# ABP Audit Logging

## Configuration
```csharp
Configure<AbpAuditingOptions>(options =>
{
    options.IsEnabled = true;
    options.IsEnabledForAnonymousUsers = false;
    options.IsEnabledForGetRequests = false;
});
```

## Entity Audit
Enable entity change tracking:
```csharp
Configure<AbpAuditingOptions>(options =>
{
    options.EntityHistorySelectors.AddAllEntities();
    // Or selective:
    options.EntityHistorySelectors.Add(
        new NamedTypeSelector("MyEntities", type => typeof(IEntity).IsAssignableFrom(type))
    );
});
```

## Attributes
- `[Audited]` - Enable audit logging for entity/service/method
- `[DisableAuditing]` - Disable audit logging
- Use on properties to exclude sensitive data (like passwords)

## Example Entity
```csharp
[Audited]
public class MyEntity : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; set; }
    
    [DisableAuditing]
    public string SensitiveData { get; set; }
}
```

## Accessing Audit Log
```csharp
var currentAuditLogScope = _auditingManager.Current;
currentAuditLogScope?.Log.Comments.Add("Custom comment");
currentAuditLogScope?.Log.SetProperty("CustomProperty", value);
```
